@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-markdown-semantic-parity
The parser boundary MUST preserve Android's existing CommonMark 0.24.0 feature
semantics, including tables and alignment, autolinks, task lists, strike, emphasis,
links and images, headings, code blocks, breaks and inert HTML nodes. Android MUST
retain its current parser and extensions; the Apple adapter MUST consume a proven
GFM syntax tree and MUST NOT replace Markdown parsing with regular expressions.
Shared goldens MUST run on both platforms, with direct parser parity on the JVM.
Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and DESIGN.md rules 95 and 96.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] shared-markdown-stays-ui-free
Semantic nodes and parsing MUST have no Compose, Android, transport or native UI
dependencies. Parser objects MUST NOT escape into the shared renderer or feature
state. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 chosen shared-domain/shared-presentation boundaries.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] github-html-reads-as-github
After parsing, raw HTML in Markdown (review comments, bot summaries) MUST be read as
GitHub shows it: an HTML block as the Markdown it holds, a `<details>` around Markdown
blocks as one fold with its summary as the title (open when it says `open`), and
inline `<img>`, `<picture>`, `<a href>`, `<b>`, `<i>`, `<s>`, `<code>` and `<br>` as
images, links, emphasis, code and breaks. Comments and other tags MUST drop away with
their text kept. Nothing MAY run as script. A `> [!NOTE]` alert (and TIP, IMPORTANT,
WARNING, CAUTION) MUST keep its quote with its title in bold on its own line. Source: Tavi's 28 Oct 2026 request to check every screen, "particularly the diff" and "the markdown rendering, for example, for the description";
Devin's "Learn more" fold showed loose over text that never folded, and its badge vanished.
